not comfort his  captain in times like this  he could not really call himself a true  straw hat this  shows us that his acceptance and  relationship with luffy has  now gone full circle over the course of  the two years usop then tries to get as  strong as he can for his captain  and aims to become a true sniper worthy  of fighting for the future pirate king  the last arc that we have to take a look  at in order to understand usop's  character development is dressrosa  this is the second major turning point  for usopp in the story so far  when stuck in the underground harbor  robin gets turned into a toy  leaving usop as the last remaining straw  hat to stand against treble  and sugar the tontara who are being  wiped out by treble  put all their hopes into solando another  character created by usopp to hide  behind  this puts immense stress on usopp that  has been building up for the majority of  the arc  finally he can't handle it anymore and  same as he did in orlon park  he runs away in order to hide tragically  right here usa represents one of the  main themes of dressrosa  deception all this time doflamingo had  been deceiving the tontata  and now they have to find out that usual  was essentially doing the same  yet same as he did at arlong park ustop  realizes that this is not who he really  wants to  be he comes out and tells the tontada  the truth  he is usopp the sniper of the straw hat  pirates  and he will be their hero in this moment  having neither soga king nor usolando  left to hide behind he finally overcomes  another one of his great insecurities  and  stands against treble and sugar as  himself  he no longer needs a mask to hide behind  he then successfully saves the tontata  and even manages to knock out sugar  twice  this newly found courage and  self-confidence are almost directly  rewarded by the awakening of his  observation haki  that he then uses to save luffy and law  finally he was also able to prove his  worth for luffy  not to the others but to himself and  confirm for himself  his right for being part of the crew


